1
00:00:09,622 --> 00:00:14,227
KOCHIKAME

2
00:00:14,227 --> 00:00:17,297
Ah, summer's here again

3
00:00:17,397 --> 00:00:20,133
It's come, it's arrived, it's here

4
00:00:20,233 --> 00:00:23,236
Ah, summer's here again

5
00:00:23,436 --> 00:00:25,805
It's come, it's arrived, here it is!

6
00:00:25,905 --> 00:00:28,975
Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves

7
00:00:29,108 --> 00:00:31,678
Here they come on the southern wind

8
00:00:31,778 --> 00:00:34,948
Big boobs, small boobs, tiny boobs and middle-size boobs

9
00:00:35,048 --> 00:00:38,017
At the beach Jiggle, jiggle, jiggle!

10
00:00:38,017 --> 00:00:41,054
Ah, summer's here again

11
00:00:41,187 --> 00:00:43,856
It's come, it's arrived, it's here

12
00:00:44,057 --> 00:00:46,893
Ah, summer's here again

13
00:00:47,026 --> 00:00:49,495
It's come, it's arrived, it's here already!

14
00:00:49,562 --> 00:00:52,665
Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves

15
00:00:52,765 --> 00:00:55,535
Here they come on the southern wind

16
00:00:55,635 --> 00:00:58,605
Big butts, small butts, tiny butts and middle-size butts

17
00:00:58,705 --> 00:01:03,042
At the beach Bounce, bounce, bounce!

18
00:01:06,212 --> 00:01:14,988
Here they come on the southern wind

19
00:01:18,024 --> 00:01:21,628
Bouncing at the beach Jiggling at the beach

20
00:01:23,396 --> 00:01:24,497
Want you!

21
00:01:28,167 --> 00:01:34,173
KANKICHI RYOTSU, MAVERICK POLICE OFFICER

22
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:55,461
KAMEARI, 3RD DISTRICT

23
00:02:06,005 --> 00:02:07,006
He's coming!

24
00:02:15,548 --> 00:02:17,317
Here he comes!

25
00:02:19,686 --> 00:02:20,987
Oops!

26
00:02:22,455 --> 00:02:24,957
You're full of energy this morning, Ryo-san!

27
00:02:26,326 --> 00:02:27,627
I'm gonna be late!

28
00:02:28,027 --> 00:02:30,797
Who would park their car in a place like this?

29
00:02:30,997 --> 00:02:32,865
Must be an inconsiderate jerk.

30
00:02:33,066 --> 00:02:34,867
Get out of the way!

31
00:02:35,134 --> 00:02:35,968
What?

32
00:02:36,202 --> 00:02:37,236
Coming through!

33
00:02:47,046 --> 00:02:48,247
No way!

34
00:02:48,614 --> 00:02:50,016
Stop right there!

35
00:03:01,227 --> 00:03:02,895
Who is that guy?

36
00:03:03,096 --> 00:03:04,597
Kankichi Ryotsu.

37
00:03:04,797 --> 00:03:06,432
He's the ugliest, rudest,

38
00:03:06,766 --> 00:03:10,436
most irresponsible caveman in all of Kameari!

39
00:03:11,137 --> 00:03:15,575
Stop that bicycle at once, you neanderthal!

40
00:03:17,577 --> 00:03:21,748
Think you can catch Kankichi Ryotsu, do you?

41
00:03:22,315 --> 00:03:25,218
My current speed is over 30 kilometers an hour.

42
00:03:26,686 --> 00:03:28,788
40, 50…

43
00:03:29,055 --> 00:03:30,857
60, 70…

44
00:03:31,057 --> 00:03:32,925
80!

45
00:03:34,193 --> 00:03:37,397
The rev counter is pushing into the red zone of 10,000 rpm.

46
00:03:37,764 --> 00:03:41,067
Hang on for a 90-degree turn!

47
00:03:45,805 --> 00:03:47,673
He's terrible.

48
00:03:47,907 --> 00:03:48,708
Darn it!

49
00:04:07,994 --> 00:04:09,562
KAMEARI PARK POLICE STATION

50
00:04:22,008 --> 00:04:24,377
Yes! I made it!

51
00:04:25,645 --> 00:04:27,346
I arrived on time!

52
00:04:30,817 --> 00:04:32,485
All's well that ends well!

53
00:04:32,685 --> 00:04:34,787
It didn't end well, Ryo-san.

54
00:04:34,987 --> 00:04:39,125
You broke the window. The chief will be furious again.

55
00:04:39,826 --> 00:04:45,097
I've been watering those flowers every day and they've finally bloomed.

56
00:04:45,498 --> 00:04:47,567
If you touch them again, I won't forgive you.

57
00:04:48,734 --> 00:04:50,136
She never stops nagging.

58
00:04:51,137 --> 00:04:55,875
The chief isn't even here yet. He needs to get it together.

59
00:04:56,876 --> 00:05:02,148
The person at the top should get here at least 30 minutes before the rest of us.

60
00:05:02,715 --> 00:05:04,617
Ryo… Ryo-san…

61
00:05:04,817 --> 00:05:07,086
What's wrong, Terai?

62
00:05:07,286 --> 00:05:08,154
Ah!

63
00:05:21,567 --> 00:05:22,735
Chief!

64
00:05:23,436 --> 00:05:25,137
You're here bright and early.

65
00:05:25,338 --> 00:05:29,976
I really admire how you commute for over two hours from way out in the sticks.

66
00:05:30,176 --> 00:05:32,445
You're a role model for all police officers.

67
00:05:32,912 --> 00:05:34,714
You idiot!

68
00:05:37,216 --> 00:05:39,418
Why did you shout at me?

69
00:05:39,652 --> 00:05:42,088
I wasn't late this morning.

70
00:05:42,255 --> 00:05:45,224
I slid in a whole minute early

71
00:05:45,424 --> 00:05:47,393
You moron!

72
00:05:49,762 --> 00:05:53,866
Even at your age, you still behave just like a naughty kid!

73
00:05:54,066 --> 00:05:56,402
How many apology letters have you had to write?

74
00:05:56,602 --> 00:05:58,404
Are you trying to set a record?

75
00:05:58,604 --> 00:06:01,007
That's why you can't get a wife.

76
00:06:01,007 --> 00:06:03,576
Live your life more steadily!

77
00:06:03,943 --> 00:06:07,613
My favorite enka song says it best…

78
00:06:09,248 --> 00:06:14,053
One step in one day Three steps in three days

79
00:06:14,253 --> 00:06:17,757
Three steps forward And two steps backward

80
00:06:17,957 --> 00:06:18,824
That's it.

81
00:06:19,025 --> 00:06:22,094
Wonderful! You sang it as well as Kiyoko Suizenji!

82
00:06:22,495 --> 00:06:26,065
I agree. We take three steps forward and two steps back in life.

83
00:06:26,265 --> 00:06:28,768
So you may as well take one step then relax.

84
00:06:28,935 --> 00:06:30,937
You idiot!

85
00:06:33,773 --> 00:06:38,477
I was foolish to try to teach you to have some humility in life.

86
00:06:40,513 --> 00:06:42,315
I'm getting a headache.

87
00:06:44,283 --> 00:06:45,318
Finally, he's gone.

88
00:06:45,818 --> 00:06:47,653
He's always calling me an idiot.

89
00:06:47,853 --> 00:06:50,323
Sometimes I think it's the only word he knows.

90
00:06:53,926 --> 00:06:58,197
Oh, you're back, Chief. Did you forget something?

91
00:07:01,667 --> 00:07:04,503
SALARY

92
00:07:01,767 --> 00:07:04,403
Oh, today is payday.

93
00:07:04,804 --> 00:07:07,306
I don't want to give you it, but I have no choice.

94
00:07:07,506 --> 00:07:08,474
Listen up, Ryotsu.

95
00:07:08,674 --> 00:07:11,944
When you get some money, you shouldn't spend it right away.

96
00:07:12,144 --> 00:07:15,915
You must think about the future, and use it wisely.

97
00:07:17,116 --> 00:07:18,017
Yes, sir.

98
00:07:22,288 --> 00:07:25,124
I can buy another radio-controlled vehicle.

99
00:07:27,493 --> 00:07:28,995
What are you doing, Chief?

100
00:07:29,195 --> 00:07:32,198
That's one month's worth of my sweat and tears!

101
00:07:32,698 --> 00:07:36,736
It's to fix the broken door, the window and the bicycle.

102
00:07:37,536 --> 00:07:39,105
He's such a tight-ass.

103
00:07:39,305 --> 00:07:41,607
Never mind. This is still enough.

104
00:07:41,807 --> 00:07:44,176
We've all been waiting for payday!

105
00:07:44,377 --> 00:07:45,478
What?

106
00:07:48,848 --> 00:07:51,717
We're here to collect the money you owe us.

107
00:07:52,585 --> 00:07:55,988
Jeez, every store owner in town is here!

108
00:07:56,188 --> 00:07:57,757
Damn, I guess I need to…

109
00:07:58,357 --> 00:08:00,126
-Run! -Hold it!

110
00:08:00,326 --> 00:08:01,327
Chief!

111
00:08:01,527 --> 00:08:04,397
Terai, grab his legs!

112
00:08:04,997 --> 00:08:06,165
Yes, sir.

113
00:08:06,565 --> 00:08:07,867
Let me go!

114
00:08:08,067 --> 00:08:10,703
Terai, get your hands off me!

115
00:08:12,004 --> 00:08:14,206
Everyone, please take what you're owed.

116
00:08:14,407 --> 00:08:15,708
Hands off!

117
00:08:16,075 --> 00:08:17,376
Sorry, Ryo-san.

118
00:08:17,576 --> 00:08:21,247
I'll take 38,000 yen for the video games and plastic models.

119
00:08:21,747 --> 00:08:24,216
22,000 yen for the noodles you ate.

120
00:08:24,884 --> 00:08:26,952
28,000 yen for the beer and whiskey.

121
00:08:27,186 --> 00:08:28,688
Have some restraint!

122
00:08:29,055 --> 00:08:29,922
Thank you.

123
00:08:30,122 --> 00:08:32,525
18,000 yen for all the set meals.

124
00:08:33,225 --> 00:08:34,427
3,000 yen for the fishing rod.

125
00:08:34,627 --> 00:08:36,562
27,000 yen for the comic books.

126
00:08:36,762 --> 00:08:38,297
Thank you very much!

127
00:08:40,433 --> 00:08:42,935
KAMEARI PARK POLICE STATION

128
00:08:43,335 --> 00:08:44,804
Only 150 yen left.

129
00:08:45,638 --> 00:08:48,207
I can't survive one month with this.

130
00:08:48,407 --> 00:08:49,942
It serves you right.

131
00:08:50,142 --> 00:08:53,212
That's why I told you to live your life more steadily.

132
00:08:53,412 --> 00:08:54,246
Chief!

133
00:08:54,847 --> 00:08:56,215
I won't give you an advance!

134
00:08:56,415 --> 00:08:58,984
Live on that money for one month like a man.

135
00:08:59,185 --> 00:09:00,386
Oh, no!

136
00:09:00,586 --> 00:09:04,256
You two mustn't lend him any money either, okay?

137
00:09:05,057 --> 00:09:07,793
I cannot afford to with my mortgage payments.

138
00:09:08,127 --> 00:09:11,997
Don't worry, Ryo-chan. I'm sure you can survive on that money.

139
00:09:12,298 --> 00:09:15,468
Yes, don't indulge him. It's for his own sake.

140
00:09:15,668 --> 00:09:20,106
Chief, please lend me 50,000 yen. Or even 30,000.

141
00:09:20,306 --> 00:09:22,775
How about 20,000 yen?

142
00:09:23,342 --> 00:09:24,276
10,000 then.

143
00:09:24,643 --> 00:09:27,146
At least let me borrow 1,000 yen!

144
00:09:27,346 --> 00:09:28,814
No way!

145
00:09:31,217 --> 00:09:32,318
Skinflint!

146
00:09:34,286 --> 00:09:36,088
I won't ask any of you again.

147
00:09:36,288 --> 00:09:40,493
I'd rather starve to death than beg such cold-hearted people!

148
00:09:40,693 --> 00:09:44,263
Okay then. Don't forget what you just said.

149
00:09:44,663 --> 00:09:47,633
We won't help you if you get hungry and beg us.

150
00:09:50,736 --> 00:09:55,007
I'll live a life of luxury on this 150 yen!

151
00:09:55,608 --> 00:09:56,642
Like squabbling kids.

152
00:09:56,842 --> 00:09:57,977
They really are.

153
00:10:10,523 --> 00:10:13,025
My stomach always knows the correct time.

154
00:10:14,994 --> 00:10:15,828
Hmm?

155
00:10:19,165 --> 00:10:21,267
Yes! Reiko is not here.

156
00:10:30,676 --> 00:10:33,913
While she's away, I can eat her lunch.

157
00:10:39,585 --> 00:10:42,688
Ouch!

158
00:10:43,055 --> 00:10:48,894
Who was it who'd rather starve to death than beg us for help?

159
00:10:50,196 --> 00:10:53,532
Dang it! She knew my behavior patterns.

160
00:11:02,575 --> 00:11:04,944
Terai, give me your lunch!

161
00:11:05,177 --> 00:11:07,613
No way, this is mine.

162
00:11:07,813 --> 00:11:08,948
Give it to me!

163
00:11:09,248 --> 00:11:12,918
Ryo-chan, taking someone else's property is theft.

164
00:11:13,185 --> 00:11:13,953
Shut up!

165
00:11:13,953 --> 00:11:16,255
I don't see his name written on the rice.

166
00:11:16,956 --> 00:11:18,457
Hand it over!

167
00:11:20,192 --> 00:11:22,428
Ryo-chan, cut it out!

168
00:11:22,628 --> 00:11:24,897
-Give it here. -I said no!

169
00:11:25,097 --> 00:11:26,398
Terai!

170
00:11:40,212 --> 00:11:43,983
Damn you, Reiko! But I'll get it no matter what.

171
00:11:53,592 --> 00:11:56,528
His passion for food is incredible.

172
00:12:02,668 --> 00:12:04,003
Damn it!

173
00:12:12,478 --> 00:12:15,514
If I see you again, I'll turn you into a scarf!

174
00:12:24,056 --> 00:12:25,758
I'm starving.

175
00:12:26,792 --> 00:12:29,128
There's gotta be something I can eat…

176
00:12:29,295 --> 00:12:31,797
Yes! Rice cakes!

177
00:12:32,598 --> 00:12:34,967
There's always some food if you look hard enough.

178
00:12:35,868 --> 00:12:38,637
Pour in a little bit of ponzu sauce.

179
00:12:39,004 --> 00:12:40,506
Oops, I added too much.

180
00:12:40,706 --> 00:12:42,174
It'll be too sour now.

181
00:12:42,374 --> 00:12:44,877
I'd better add some salt.

182
00:12:45,744 --> 00:12:48,447
Oh, no. That's way too much.

183
00:12:48,647 --> 00:12:50,015
Let's add some sugar.

184
00:12:51,717 --> 00:12:55,154
Oh well, I guess this'll have to do.

185
00:12:55,354 --> 00:12:59,024
As a final touch, some tonkatsu sauce.

186
00:12:59,325 --> 00:13:01,327
My signature hotpot is complete!

187
00:13:01,527 --> 00:13:04,496
I found some leftover rice cakes from New Year's.

188
00:13:04,897 --> 00:13:08,534
What? Weren't they covered with mold already?

189
00:13:09,335 --> 00:13:12,037
So? Mushrooms are mold too, but you eat them, right?

190
00:13:12,304 --> 00:13:16,008
I added some hydrangea leaves for perfect nutritional balance.

191
00:13:16,742 --> 00:13:18,978
Are hydrangea leaves even edible?

192
00:13:19,345 --> 00:13:22,915
Sure they are. If they look nice, they must taste good too.

193
00:13:24,883 --> 00:13:27,987
It's lacking a bit of color.

194
00:13:30,556 --> 00:13:33,325
Ryo-san, those are Reiko-san's flowers.

195
00:13:33,525 --> 00:13:35,728
Color is important in cooking.

196
00:13:37,696 --> 00:13:39,498
Time to eat.

197
00:13:40,532 --> 00:13:42,034
Huh?

198
00:13:42,668 --> 00:13:47,006
Ryo-chan, what have you done?

199
00:13:49,408 --> 00:13:51,477
I told you not to touch them again!

200
00:13:51,677 --> 00:13:52,544
You barbarian!

201
00:13:59,885 --> 00:14:01,253
Damn it.

202
00:14:01,453 --> 00:14:04,223
At least leave some change for me. Skinflints!

203
00:14:07,126 --> 00:14:10,396
I'm so hungry.

204
00:14:16,068 --> 00:14:17,002
That smells like…

205
00:14:22,174 --> 00:14:24,543
Yes, that's it!

206
00:14:25,277 --> 00:14:28,547
It's Junpei and Kappei, the tofu maker's kids.

207
00:14:34,286 --> 00:14:35,788
Nice, Junpei!

208
00:14:35,988 --> 00:14:38,157
-Go for it, Junpei! -Come on!

209
00:14:38,357 --> 00:14:39,558
Keep it up!

210
00:14:39,758 --> 00:14:42,227
Well, well, well. Having fun, kids?

211
00:14:42,428 --> 00:14:44,863
Hey, you're pretty skillful.

212
00:14:46,265 --> 00:14:47,766
That takoyaki looks tasty.

213
00:14:47,966 --> 00:14:50,502
Think you could challenge me, Junpei?

214
00:14:51,136 --> 00:14:53,005
Challenge you?

215
00:14:53,238 --> 00:14:55,607
That's right. One round each at this game.

216
00:14:55,808 --> 00:14:59,144
If I win, I get this takoyaki.

217
00:15:00,145 --> 00:15:01,513
If you lose?

218
00:15:01,847 --> 00:15:06,985
I give you anything from my collection of plastic models and video games.

219
00:15:07,186 --> 00:15:08,987
Really? Plastic models?

220
00:15:09,655 --> 00:15:11,957
You up for it, Junpei?

221
00:15:12,758 --> 00:15:13,692
Sure!

222
00:15:14,193 --> 00:15:15,727
Come on, Junpei!

223
00:15:15,928 --> 00:15:17,796
You can do it!

224
00:15:20,766 --> 00:15:22,134
The kids are lively today.

225
00:15:22,334 --> 00:15:23,335
Oh, Ryo-san.

226
00:15:28,907 --> 00:15:29,775
Yes!

227
00:15:29,975 --> 00:15:33,345
Your score is 980 out of 1000 points.

228
00:15:33,545 --> 00:15:34,913
Well done, kid.

229
00:15:35,147 --> 00:15:36,615
Okay, it's my turn.

230
00:15:40,252 --> 00:15:41,286
Start!

231
00:15:41,553 --> 00:15:46,625
My special technique, Crimson Bombardment!

232
00:16:00,005 --> 00:16:01,006
We got lucky!

233
00:16:02,007 --> 00:16:04,877
Hi-yah! Backward version!

234
00:16:09,214 --> 00:16:10,015
No way!

235
00:16:17,256 --> 00:16:18,423
He got the maximum!

236
00:16:18,657 --> 00:16:19,725
Wow!

237
00:16:21,493 --> 00:16:22,294
Impressed?

238
00:16:22,995 --> 00:16:26,265
-I lost. -You shouldn't have done it.

239
00:16:26,798 --> 00:16:29,835
Okay, give me your takoyaki as we promised.

240
00:16:42,748 --> 00:16:44,116
Junpei!

241
00:16:44,516 --> 00:16:46,218
What a jerk!

242
00:16:47,085 --> 00:16:48,387
Are you all right?

243
00:16:50,355 --> 00:16:52,658
Arrest the driver, Ryo-san!

244
00:16:52,858 --> 00:16:53,926
Leave it to me!

245
00:16:54,126 --> 00:16:56,428
Stop right there!

246
00:17:00,265 --> 00:17:02,568
Hold it!

247
00:17:03,835 --> 00:17:05,037
Yikes!

248
00:17:13,245 --> 00:17:14,746
Let me use your bike!

249
00:17:15,948 --> 00:17:18,183
Turn on the ultra-power-turbo!

250
00:17:18,717 --> 00:17:20,185
Ryo-san!

251
00:17:31,697 --> 00:17:34,266
He's chasing us on a bike!

252
00:17:34,466 --> 00:17:35,667
He'll never catch up.

253
00:17:35,867 --> 00:17:38,604
I'm not getting arrested for just grazing some kid.

254
00:17:55,153 --> 00:17:56,588
How's that possible?

255
00:17:56,788 --> 00:17:59,057
I won't let you get away!

256
00:18:13,605 --> 00:18:16,675
Damn it! I'll get ahead of him.

257
00:18:17,376 --> 00:18:20,345
Missile jump!

258
00:18:26,685 --> 00:18:30,188
KAME-NO-YU BATHHOUSE

259
00:18:42,868 --> 00:18:44,736
Shoot! Time for a shortcut!

260
00:18:51,376 --> 00:18:53,378
Oh, no! Wrong way!

261
00:18:56,548 --> 00:18:58,283
What are you doing, Ryo-san?

262
00:18:58,717 --> 00:19:00,786
Sorry, I'm on duty!

263
00:19:10,028 --> 00:19:11,063
See you later!

264
00:19:26,578 --> 00:19:28,046
Look what you did, Ryo-san!

265
00:19:28,613 --> 00:19:30,582
I'm chasing a criminal.

266
00:19:34,386 --> 00:19:36,254
Stop the car!

267
00:19:39,257 --> 00:19:40,792
Gotcha!

268
00:19:41,727 --> 00:19:44,262
He's still coming. Speed up!

269
00:19:44,463 --> 00:19:45,797
Why won't he give up?

270
00:19:50,135 --> 00:19:52,938
Who do you think I am?

271
00:20:01,146 --> 00:20:03,415
We're driving at 80 kilometers an hour!

272
00:20:03,715 --> 00:20:04,716
Faster!

273
00:20:13,425 --> 00:20:15,227
Watch out, stupid dog!

274
00:20:32,177 --> 00:20:34,045
Looks like he's finally given up.

275
00:20:34,446 --> 00:20:35,647
Oh, my God!

276
00:20:35,914 --> 00:20:36,715
What?

277
00:20:39,618 --> 00:20:42,087
Stop the car, bastard!

278
00:20:43,255 --> 00:20:45,757
This guy is a monster!

279
00:21:12,017 --> 00:21:13,852
He's nowhere in sight.

280
00:21:14,052 --> 00:21:15,187
We made it, Ken.

281
00:21:15,387 --> 00:21:17,856
We sure showed him!

282
00:21:26,498 --> 00:21:28,133
Aha, an exit!

283
00:21:37,876 --> 00:21:38,877
Ryo-san!

284
00:21:51,156 --> 00:21:52,958
He's arrested the criminal.

285
00:21:53,158 --> 00:21:54,426
Nice work!

286
00:21:56,294 --> 00:21:57,896
You bastard!

287
00:21:58,396 --> 00:22:00,866
I'm sorry. I'll never do it again!

288
00:22:02,868 --> 00:22:04,636
You owe me some takoyaki!

289
00:22:05,537 --> 00:22:06,605
What?

290
00:22:06,838 --> 00:22:11,276
I'm talking about takoyaki. You ruined mine!

291
00:22:19,384 --> 00:22:21,586
You did great, Ryo-chan.

292
00:22:21,987 --> 00:22:25,323
You caught a criminal for the first time in eight years. Well done!

293
00:22:25,557 --> 00:22:29,094
You know what they say, "Wise talons hide their hawks."

294
00:22:29,728 --> 00:22:32,097
Actually, it's "Wise hawks hide their talons."

295
00:22:32,297 --> 00:22:34,065
But it doesn't suit you.

296
00:22:34,432 --> 00:22:35,567
Ryo-san!

297
00:22:36,368 --> 00:22:37,802
Hey, Junpei.

298
00:22:38,203 --> 00:22:39,604
Is your leg all right?

299
00:22:40,405 --> 00:22:42,607
It's just a scratch.

300
00:22:43,074 --> 00:22:46,077
Next time, I'll win against you for sure!

301
00:22:46,578 --> 00:22:50,448
All right. Make sure you practice hard, Junpei.

302
00:22:51,783 --> 00:22:54,586
Oh right, I still haven't eaten anything.

303
00:22:55,086 --> 00:23:00,592
I heard that driver was a notorious traffic violator.

304
00:23:00,792 --> 00:23:04,796
You might even receive a special monetary award for arresting him.

305
00:23:05,063 --> 00:23:06,865
Some money? Awesome!

306
00:23:07,065 --> 00:23:09,067
I'll be able to survive this month!

307
00:23:09,267 --> 00:23:11,603
Is Ryotsu here?

308
00:23:11,803 --> 00:23:13,104
Here it comes.

309
00:23:15,106 --> 00:23:15,807
Yes, sir!

310
00:23:15,807 --> 00:23:19,578
Kameari's finest police officer and scourge of hit-and-run criminals,

311
00:23:19,778 --> 00:23:23,415
Kankichi Ryotsu at your service.

312
00:23:25,817 --> 00:23:28,086
Do you have my reward money?

313
00:23:28,286 --> 00:23:29,955
You idiot!

314
00:23:32,657 --> 00:23:34,326
Look outside.

315
00:23:38,797 --> 00:23:43,535
I heard you caused trouble for the local residents again.

316
00:23:43,735 --> 00:23:47,505
You must pay for their damages from your next month's salary!

317
00:23:47,872 --> 00:23:49,975
You can't be serious!

318
00:23:50,375 --> 00:23:55,013
Please spare me, Chief!

319
00:23:55,146 --> 00:23:57,415
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

320
00:23:57,415 --> 00:24:00,752
1 CAR, 2 BICYCLES, 7 FLOWERS 5 T-SHIRTS, 2 TRASHCANS, 30 TILES

321
00:24:00,986 --> 00:24:03,088
5 FENCES TO FIX

322
00:24:06,024 --> 00:24:09,327
A new police officer is assigned to Kameari Park Police Station.

323
00:24:09,527 --> 00:24:12,797
Apparently, he's the only heir to the super-rich Nakagawa Corporation.

324
00:24:12,998 --> 00:24:16,835
How can such a spoiled brat work as a police officer?

325
00:24:17,102 --> 00:24:23,074
A ROOKIE COP FROM THE HEAVENS

326
00:24:17,102 --> 00:24:23,074
NEXT EPISODE

327
00:24:32,384 --> 00:24:36,688
Let's keep smiling always

328
00:24:37,255 --> 00:24:40,925
Even when things go wrong

329
00:24:41,126 --> 00:24:45,397
Keep a pretty smile on your face

330
00:24:45,997 --> 00:24:50,468
And go out as if nothing happened

331
00:24:51,002 --> 00:24:54,072
Hey, show me your smile

332
00:24:54,272 --> 00:24:58,777
You did nothing wrong

333
00:24:59,678 --> 00:25:02,747
Hey, show me your smile

334
00:25:02,947 --> 00:25:06,885
Just like you did before, yeah

335
00:25:07,318 --> 00:25:11,556
I want you to smile always

336
00:25:12,223 --> 00:25:16,728
A woman with a frown isn't pretty

337
00:25:17,195 --> 00:25:22,767
So you should smile as soon as you can

338
00:25:23,368 --> 00:25:26,504
It's the grown-up thing to do

339
00:25:39,050 --> 00:25:43,988
KOCHIKAME SEE YOU NEXT TIME!
